# Extension metadata. These XB- fields are the ONLY thing the WebUI's
# extension catalog reads (configurator's extensions/catalog.py builds every
# card from the apt record) -- omit one and it silently falls back: no
# Extension-Name shows the raw package name, no Extension-Category files a
# player under "Tools". dpkg strips the XB- prefix in the built record.
XB-Hifiberry-Extension: yes
XB-Extension-Name: Spotify Soloist
XB-Extension-Category: player
XB-Extension-Needs-Reboot: no
# Served by hifiberry-webui itself, so this resolves on a device with no
# internet access; an external URL would leave a broken image offline.
XB-Extension-Icon-Url: /images/svg/spotify.svg
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 python3, python3-websocket, curl, ca-certificates,
 hifiberry-configurator (>= 2.17.6), hifiberry-audiocontrol (>= 0.9.0)
Description: Spotify Soloist player for HiFiBerryOS
 Runs Spotify Soloist as a Spotify Connect endpoint and bridges its local
 WebSocket API to audiocontrol, providing metadata, artwork, queue and
 transport control.
 .
 This package does not contain the Spotify Soloist binary, which may not be
 redistributed. It is downloaded from Spotify on first use, and each user must
 supply their own Soloist API key from the Spotify for Developers dashboard.
 A Spotify Premium account is required.
